Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the xHCI driver scheduling work to clear the TT buffer while the USB core was simultaneously freeing and reallocating a new device during enumeration. This led to a use-after-free condition where the work could dereference pointers to already freed endpoint and device structures, resulting in potential crashes or undefined behavior.

