The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
udev = (struct usb_device *)host_ep->hcpriv;
vdev = xhci->devs[udev->slot_id];
ep = &vdev->eps[ep_index];
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the xHCI driver schedules work to clear the TT buffer while the USB core is freeing and reallocating a new device. If the work is executed after the device has been freed, it can dereference pointers to already freed endpoint and device structures, leading to a use-after-free condition.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ep->ep_state & EP_CLEARING_TT) {
    spin_unlock_irqrestore(&xhci->lock, flags);
    schedule_timeout_uninterruptible(1);
    goto rescan;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the xHCI driver waits for the `hub_tt_work` to finish clearing the hub TT before proceeding to disable the endpoint. This prevents the dereferencing of pointers to freed structures, thus avoiding the use-after-free condition.

